WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:02.450
- Okay, this is my
first solo cooking demo.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.640
I'm not gonna lie, I'm a
little nervous and excited,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.650
but you know what, when
everything is calm and normal,

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.630
it means you've done it.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.291
A healthy amount of fear is good.

00:00:10.291 --> 00:00:11.760
(audience cheering)

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.200
Thank you.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.760
What I wanted to cook for you guys today

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.410
is a pasta that is really
near and dear to me.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.930
I could eat pasta every
single day of my life.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.930
I have the metabolism of a sloth
who's asleep at the switch.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.050
So unfortunately I cannot.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.090
I love food, but what I've tried to do,

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.430
'cause I've been on a
wrecking ball pendulum

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.340
swinging back and forth, heavy,
thin, heavy, thin for me.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.730
Everybody's body is different.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.070
There is no diet, one size fits all.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.240
And I also think that I've
tried to educate myself

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.470
to make healthy alternatives
of dishes I love.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.590
Because when I was doing
the chicken and broccoli

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.350
type of diet with
working out all the time,

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.720
here's what happened.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.240
I would go off the rails,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.780
and then my pendulum would
swing all the way that way.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.870
I've tried to find foods that actually

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.830
are just like the foods I love,

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.770
but very healthy versions of them.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.310
I'm gonna make a spaghetti
today that's actually made

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.053
with, secret ingredient, chickpeas.

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:13.920
This pasta has changed my life,

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.750
and the truth is the way we digest food

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.240
is a lot of gluten-free and
rice alternatives to pasta

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.410
are a little inflammatory.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.730
With this sauce, this
is just a simple sauce.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.380
And I always wanted to be that kind of guy

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.700
who made simple sauces at home,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.240
but I'm not like sexy in the kitchen.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.080
I'm a little bird brained.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.920
But this, if I can do it,
trust me, anyone can do it.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.550
I also love cooking solo.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.590
I love when recipes give
the right ratios for that.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.110
If you go on our website,

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:46.580
you're going to be able to
get this for four to six,

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.200
but also one to two.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.570
Jose Andres is on the show.

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:52.930
And he said, throw your
garlic in with the peel on.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.730
And that way it won't burn.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:58.140
Turns out, he's Jose Andres for a reason.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.390
I've been doing it now,
and it has changed my game.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.930
All right, so we're
going to get this going.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.720
And when your oil is sort of sizzling,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.070
you're going to take cherry tomatoes.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.937
The longest thing honestly--

00:02:07.937 --> 00:02:10.210
(tomatoes sizzling)
(audience cheering)

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.510
Yeah!

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.400
Oh, I told Jose Andres, I'm
also turning my heat down.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.160
Okay. Calm down.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.620
But longest thing that actually takes here

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.160
is cutting the cherry tomatoes.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.060
This whole sauce should take 10 minutes.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.200
I love layering.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.410
This pasta can also be
made as fresh as you want,

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:31.020
or it can be made as a
complete pantry dish.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.950
All you have to do is
take your dried spices.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.780
I've got cherry tomatoes, basil, salt.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.550
Now, my secret tip is I
love a little harissa paste.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.330
It's a Tunisian spice.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.240
And I do sort of like Lima
bean-size things in there.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.983
And it adds this nice smoky, spicy.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:49.863
I don't have a thing.

00:02:49.863 --> 00:02:52.250
All right, I'm going right in here.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:54.200
And literally this is it.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.230
If you have dried herbs,
you can do oregano, parsley.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.700
You could even do chopped
tomatoes in a can.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.793
This can really be a staple
anytime that you want it.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.560
I'm also going to do
a little tomato paste.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.560
This, again, little Lima
bean-size dollops right in there.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.290
And then you're just going
to keep cooking it down.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.340
And eventually the cherry
tomatoes will just break open,

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.470
but they'll remain intact enough.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.960
And you're going to have what
looks like a restaurant dish.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.030
And like I said, if I can do
this, anybody can do this.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.790
Another thing that's
really great about this.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.800
If you would like to add
meatballs, go for it.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:36.050
Because the way digestion works is that

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:40.890
it doesn't process meat,
proteins, and grains very well.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.400
But because this is a chickpea flour,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.830
your stomach welcomes proteins with it.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.630
I also love to rock a
little digestive enzymes.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.720
You can find these in any
health foods store or grocery.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.370
Yeah, it just aids with digestion.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.350
And since I started eating this way,

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.770
I've actually maintained the same weight.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.860
And that is my secret.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:05.060
I have found a way to have
pleasure in the kitchen,

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.060
and my body is happy

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.140
and it's responding with something

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.830
that feels really good and empowering.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:12.780
And I'm not deprived.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.220
I'm totally enjoying myself.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.280
Shout out to The Pasta Queen, my friend,

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.600
who's a maven on Tik Tok.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.190
She says to take your ladle

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.740
to get the ultimate in bird's nest.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:22.820
And it really works.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.653
Look at this.

00:04:23.653 --> 00:04:25.670
If this was a bowl, it's perfect.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.220
So shout out to her.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.190
Ta-da! All right, I'm going to taste it.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:32.330
I hope that you guys
have enjoyed the show.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.400
Oh, beauty shot.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.540
Oh, god, I already messed
up the beauty shot.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.683
Well,
(audience cheering)

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.986
I hope that you take all the goodness

00:04:42.986 --> 00:04:45.410
that we're feeling here with you

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.580
throughout the rest of your day.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.910
That's what we're really here for

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.780
is to just spread good
energy and good cheer

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:55.165
and enjoy life and find what
all the things that are worth

00:04:55.165 --> 00:04:58.250
just being human for.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.753
Thank you very much for joining us today.

00:05:00.753 --> 00:05:03.336
(upbeat music)

